# Step 01 — Create & link ocm-role  [THE FIX]
# Account: 759945100724  OCM: stage  Date: 2026-10-12
#
# This is the step that was impossible on 301721915996 and that blocked the
# whole first attempt. The ocm-role is what authorizes the OCM organization to
# reach into the AWS account. It is per-AWS-account, and must be LINKED to the
# org. On the old account the only ocm-role was a shared CI role we would not
# touch; here the account is empty so we create our own.
#
# Role name is derived from prefix + org external ID (11009103):
#   alebedev-OCM-Role-11009103
#
# Basic (non-admin) role -- no --admin flag. Admin is only needed if you want
# OCM to auto-create operator roles on your behalf; we create those ourselves
# in step 06.
#
# Requires iam:CreateRole. The 759945100724-openshift-installer-restricted
# role the 'saml' profile assumes does have it. Linking additionally requires
# the OCM user to be able to link for the org -- it worked here.

## Command

AWS_PROFILE=saml rosa create ocm-role --prefix alebedev --mode auto -y

